# =============================================================================
# futbol-az — environment example
# =============================================================================
# v1 HAS NO SECRETS. The app makes zero network calls, has no backend, no
# analytics, no auth. This file exists only so the pattern is in place and so
# nobody is tempted to invent an untracked .env with real values in it.
#
# Rules:
#   - .env is git-ignored. This file (.env.example) is committed.
#   - Placeholder values only. Never paste a real key into this file.
#   - If a feature ever seems to need a secret, STOP and discuss it first —
#     it almost certainly means a backend crept in, which is out of scope.
#
# Anything a client app ships is public. A "secret" in an Expo bundle is
# readable by anyone who downloads the APK. There is no such thing as a
# private key in a frontend-only app.
# =============================================================================

# Expo public vars must be prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ and are BUNDLED INTO THE APP.
# Treat every value here as world-readable.

# Example only — not used in v1:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_VARIANT=development
